# Release workflow

Use when the user asks to prepare a release, bump the extension version, update the changelog for a cut, package a VSIX before publish, or create a version tag.

## Source of truth

1. Follow `.cursor/skills/prepare-release/SKILL.md` step by step.
2. Align git/tag and GitHub Release expectations with `RELEASE.md`.

## Files to keep in sync

- Bump the **root `package.json`** `version` (the one version for the whole repo), run `npm run version:sync` to mirror it into the apps, then `npm install` so the root **`package-lock.json`** follows.
- Add or finalize **`CHANGELOG.md`** and **`CHANGELOG.en.md`** (dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section; move items out of `[Unreleased]` when cutting). Version update requests must update both changelog files in the same change.

## After verification

Run the scripts from the root `package.json` listed in the skill (typically `compile`, `lint`, `test`, `build`, `package:vsix` when packaging); `compile` and `package:vsix` are extension-only; `build`, `lint` and `test` fan out to every app.

Create **`git tag v<version>`** and push only after the maintainer confirms; the tag must match the **root** `package.json` version with a leading `v`, and every app must already be synced to it (`node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check`). One tag ships the VSIX, the CLI tarball, and the desktop installers (built by the release workflow on macOS and Windows runners, with the `latest*.yml` update feed).

## Build verification test (BVT)

`npm run bvt` runs between the source checks and the packaging jobs (the `bvt` job of the release workflow); run it locally before tagging. Code in `scripts/bvt/`, data in `bvt/`. Steps: `bvt:contracts` (diff contracts — a change must carry its mandatory companion in the same tag-to-HEAD range: source ↔ both changelogs, prompt resource ↔ generated module, params file ↔ sibling schema and coding-standards row, config schema ↔ settings test, `ko.ts` ↔ `en.ts`, `.claude/rules` ↔ `.cursor/rules`, version bump ↔ changelog section); `bvt:impact` (impact map `bvt/impactMap.json` — each changed file's first matching area contributes its checks, a file no row claims fails the run, `--plan` only prints); `bvt:golden` (golden workspaces `bvt/golden/` — the built CLI drives each scenario with the mock provider and the files are compared with the snapshot after masking timestamps, uuids, hashes and the version; `reopen` scenarios run read/assemble verbs on a frozen earlier-release workspace; `-- --update` rewrites fresh snapshots, never frozen ones); `bvt:smoke` (artifact smoke — `scripts/package-release.sh` packages the VSIX, the CLI tarball and install.sh, then `scripts/bvt/smoke.sh` installs the tarball with install.sh into a scratch prefix, drives a mock work with the installed CLI and checks the VSIX contents); `bvt:smoke:desktop` (starts the built desktop app with `STORYBOARD_DESKTOP_SMOKE=1`; the workflow does it on the packaged app per platform). The canonical text is `.claude/rules/release.md`.

## Preflight before the tag

Never create a release tag without `npm run release:preflight` passing on that commit: committed tree on `main`, synced and untagged version, dated non-empty `## [<version>]` in both changelogs, then lint, tests, `npm run bvt` and the desktop smoke (`-- --package` adds this platform's packaged app). Canonical text: `.claude/rules/release.md`.
